- Inputs -> cone array, car position, velocity
- Gate cones -> remove unreliable cones (use hysteresis, aka once removed be very confident before re adding the cone)
- Crop Data -> Only keep relevant cones (cones inside box shifted forwards are kept) -> (cone limit for compute time) 
- Triangulate Cones -> Run Delauney (creates triangles covering the track)
- Filter Edges -> only keeps edges going from a blue to yellow cone (Also removes error data)
- Take midpoints -> take the midpoint of each edge (possibly waited by confidence values)
- Order midpoints -> move forward and order the midpoints 
- Clean data -> remove midpoints very close to the car and behind it. Set node 0 to current position
- Create starting data -> Use car's data to start the path along an actually possible path
- Fit spline -> fit a smooth line to the midpoints starting at node 0
- Trim path -> Trim to specified look ahead length. Sample every 0.2 meters to create discrete waypoints
- Speeds -> give each waypoint a target speed capped by the waypoints curvature 
- validate -> reject a path that leaves the track or curves too much
- output -> waypoints with speeds
